# Loaded by `next build` (Vercel sets NODE_ENV=production), NOT by `next dev`.
#
# Relative on purpose: the browser calls /api on this same Vercel domain and
# next.config.ts rewrites it to Laravel server-side, so no cross-origin request
# happens and the backend's CORS allow-list never comes into play. Putting the
# backend's absolute URL here instead would send the browser straight at
# Laravel, and CORS would break again on every new deployment URL.
#
# Local development ignores this file and uses the http://localhost:8000/api
# fallback in src/lib/api.ts, so running locally never touches the live server.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=/api
